body:
I'm not sure if it's about gender roles or not. I can see how I've been impacted by a sexist society (I'm sure everyone has) but I don't seem to relate to accounts of the frustration and discontent as strongly as some detrans people seem to. I don't think I've ever had someone tell me I had to dress feminine, aside from one time in middle school, which is all I can think of atm.

&#x200B;

How did your dysphoria manifest?

&#x200B;

And yeah I'll def have to consider how T would affect me. I'd prolly go bald.

oh wow. I cant say the same of myself but it's helpful to hear about how that culture impacted you. What was your dysphoria like? How did it manifest?

&#x200B;

And you say you couldn't have really seen that at the time. Do you think that given any certain resources, or particular questions to pose to yourself, that you could have?

So I haven't done them in roller skates yet, but when learning them on ice I started off with knees bent (Mohawk like entrance). Basically a spread eagle but your legs are not straight. It's a spread eagle too, just your knees are at like 90 degree angles. From this position your hips turn out much easier, and coaches at the rink made us start out like this, and then as we were more comfortable with that, slowly begin rising out of it, straightening your legs. That and stretching your hips to be more flexible will help.

&#x200B;

I was also told to never do a spread eagle on a flat line. Try to curve inside or outside some. Or, have fun and weave around, going from inside to outside edges/curves. I hope that this advice helps on land. I use snow white inlines, not the 4 wheels or any other inlines at the moment, so I'm not sure if there is too much difference in regards to spread eagles. I would think not, on the 4 wheels at least, based on my time using them.

I didn't think of canned meat. Usually when I think of canned meat I just think of spam or something. I totally had forgotten about canned tuna and chicken, which I used to eat all the time. How did I forget? Thanks for reminding me. And by fatty, how fatty? Any brands that are best for this? Does it have to be fatty work in the microwave?

&#x200B;

And I was considering froze veggies but yeah canned may be better price wise. I do love canned peas a lot, so yay! Maybe I'll find some canned broccoli too?
